  "body": "## What changed\n\n- The post engine reads a `lineEnding` manifest entry. The value `\"lf\"` is the default. The value `\"crlf\"` ends each line with `\\r\\n`. The engine refuses any other value by name. The engine reads the entry after `onClose`, so `onOpen` can set it from a declared option.\n- `machine.travel` gives the stated linear strokes `{X, Y, Z}` to scripts. Each value is `[min, max]` in mm, or `null`. The mirror now carries the `travel` of a linear axis. The raw door reads a vendor tree through `parse_mch`.\n- The engine publishes `programBounds` before `onOpen`. It is the XY box of the cutting records, or `null`. Arcs count at the quarter points that they pass (`machine::move_extremes`). Rapids do not count.\n- New stream records `WATERJET [ABRASIVE] [DWELL<ms>] [LAG<ms>]` and `JET ON C<id> <ROLE>` / `JET OFF C<id>`. The cl types are `cl::WaterjetCut` and `cl::JetSpan` (`crates/cl/src/cl/jet.rs`). The reader takes the `.cnc` form and the `.cl` comment form.\n- The new hooks `onJetOn` / `onJetOff` fire under a `JetLaw` (`cnc_jet.rs`). The law refuses by name: a jet with no header, an ON while a jet is on, a rapid while a jet is on, and a jet that stays on. It shares no state with the plasma `TorchLaw`.\n- `linearizeArcs = true` posts each arc as chords through `onLinear`, at `chordTolerance` mm (0.01 when unstated). The engine refuses a bad tolerance by name. The chords come from `cl::Move::segments3`. The last chord ends on the arc's end point. All chord lines map to the arc record.\n- A WCS flip on a waterjet section is refused by name, the same as for plasma.\n- New post `assets/posts/waterjet-iso.cps` (generic ISO abrasive waterjet). It writes `G20`/`G21`, `G90 G94 G17 G40`, a work offset, and `G0`/`G1`/`G2`/`G3` (or G1 chords). It writes XY only. Each contour gets: water on, `G4` valve lag, abrasive on, `G4` pierce dwell, the cut, abrasive off, water off. The four M numbers, the G4 word form, the arc form and the line ending are declared options. The default M numbers (M10/M11, M12/M13) are placeholders, and the post header says so.\n- The post refuses by name: an rpm (S, G95), a surface speed (G96), coolant, a section with no `WATERJET` header, a machine not declared `kind: waterjet`, a rotary, a cycle, a Z cutting move, and a cut outside the stated `machine.travel`.\n- Docs: `docs/CNC-INTERMEDIATE.md` (records, properties, \"Waterjet records\") and `assets/posts/AGENTS.md` (hooks, sheet-cutting seams, the waterjet post).\n- Decision record: `docs/decisions/1882-waterjet-post.md`.\n\n## Cause\n\nThis is new work for #1882. The engine wrote only `\\n` lines. It did not publish linear travel or a cut box. It had no waterjet records or jet hooks, and no waterjet post was available.\n\n## Tests\n\nPins (all red on the upstream sources, 17 of 17):\n\n- `crates/post/tests/waterjet_engine.rs` (12 tests): `line_ending_crlf_ends_every_line_with_cr_lf`, `line_ending_other_words_are_refused_by_name`, `program_bounds_box_the_cut_moves_and_skip_rapids`, `machine_travel_publishes_the_linear_strokes`, `machine_travel_rides_the_mirror_and_the_raw_file`, `linearize_arcs_posts_chords_ending_on_the_arc_end`, `linearize_arcs_refuses_a_bad_tolerance_by_name`, `waterjet_records_fire_the_jet_hooks_with_their_properties`, `waterjet_records_round_trip_in_both_spellings`, `waterjet_law_refuses_what_the_stream_cannot_mean`, `waterjet_header_and_open_jet_end_with_their_section`, `waterjet_section_under_a_flipped_wcs_is_refused_by_name`.\n- `crates/post/tests/waterjet_iso_post.rs` (7 tests): the goldens `plate.nc` (mm, G2/G3) and `plate_inch_chords.nc` (inch, G1 chords, CR LF, `G4 P` ms, custom M numbers), and the refusals for spindle words, a section that is not a waterjet cut, a machine that is not a waterjet, travel, a Z cut, a dry cut and a cycle.\n- `crates/post/tests/script_waterjet_iso.rs`: the recorded-stream suite (11 refusal goldens; no recorded stream is a waterjet cut).\n- `crates/cl/src/cl/jet.rs` unit tests: line round trip, bad words, span sanity.\n\nMutation checks (one guard changed, its pin run, the guard put back): 21 of 21 red. The guards: the CR LF join, the `lineEnding` refusal, the bounds publish, the rapid skip, the arc quarter points, the travel in props, the travel in the mirror, the chord branch, the tolerance check, the jet-hook check, the jet rapid law, the jet section end, the jet fire, the WCS-flip refusal, the post rpm, CSS, header, kind, travel and Z refusals, and the order abrasive off before water off.\n\nGate: `cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main` is green: 996 steps, 0 failed (wall 30.5 min; the `cl` change reaches each dependent crate). `cargo clippy -p camcraft-cl -p camcraft-post --all-targets -- -D warnings` is clean.\n\nBranch history: the first commit was squashed onto a newer main by mistake, so it reverted nine files of the Tormach lathe G76 work (#2952). The second commit restores them from main. The net diff against main has only the #1882 files (34 files). The four new Tormach lathe test binaries pass on the combined tree. The quick gate ran on the base `768fe23f0`, before that main change; main's change since then touches none of the files of this PR.\n\n## Goldens moved\n\nNone. All goldens are new: `crates/post/tests/golden/waterjet/plate.nc`, `plate_inch_chords.nc` and the input `plate.cnc`, plus `crates/post/tests/recorded/golden/waterjet-iso/*.refusal`. No existing `.nc` or `.cl` golden changed.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- No generator writes the waterjet records yet. The `Toolpath::waterjet` field and its `.cl` dump come with the WaterjetProfile operation (#1883). The input stream here is written by hand.\n- The post is not in `posting::BUILTINS`, so the app does not offer it yet (see the decision record). A user can post with it as a file of their own (`serves = [\"waterjet\"]`).\n- The post did not run on a real waterjet control.\n\n## Overlaps\n\n- #3037 changes `engine.rs` (the `Script::load` line in `run_program_with`) and `js.rs`. This PR touches the same file, different lines. Whichever merges second refreshes.\n- #2893 changes `engine.rs` and `js.rs` (fine boring). Same file, different function. Whichever merges second refreshes.\n\nChangelog: Post: generic ISO abrasive-waterjet post (`waterjet-iso.cps`), WATERJET / JET stream records with `onJetOn` / `onJetOff`, CR LF output (`lineEnding`), `machine.travel`, `programBounds` and arc linearization (`linearizeArcs`) for scripts.\n\nEffort: high\n\nFixes #1882\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
